  "limitations": [
    "25 cities is a small number of independent geographic units; city-bootstrap intervals are wide and assume the cities are exchangeable draws from a wider population of cities, which a hand-picked list of megacities is not.",
    "One 180-day window (2025-01-01 to 2025-06-29): results may not transfer to other seasons, years, or to the opposite hemisphere's summer.",
    "The target is a MODIS daytime land-SURFACE temperature difference (urban pixel vs median of 12 rural ring points at 55–110 km), not an air-temperature UHI. Ring points can include water, mountains or other urban areas.",
    "Each 8-day LST composite is shared by up to 8 consecutive daily weather rows, so observations within a city are strongly autocorrelated; the effective sample size is the number of (city, composite) pairs, not the number of rows.",
    "Static city attributes (lat, lon, NDVI, veg class) are constant within a city, so they only identify cities; cross-city generalisation from 24 training cities is inherently limited.",
    "temp_anomaly is computed from each city's own weather over the window (no target information, no cross-city information), which is transductive for the held-out city.",
    "Leave-one-city-out does not remove spatial dependence between nearby or climatically similar cities (e.g. Delhi/Karachi, Kolkata/Dhaka) or the shared time window.",
    "The published snapshot uses the Planetary Computer MODIS mirror (MOD13A1 500 m NDVI instead of MOD13A2 1 km); the GEE collector produces a different dataset and must be re-evaluated before its numbers are quoted."
  ],
  "deployment_model": {
    "selection_procedure": "GridSearchCV over the same candidate grid, GroupKFold(n_splits=5) on all eligible cities, selection metric = mean inner-fold RMSE; refit on all eligible rows",
